e":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State's club team might be the Buckeyes' most dominant program","description":"One football team in Columbus still has national title hopes. Just not the one with Jeremiah Smith.","published":"2026-11-20T16:21:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522496/ohio-state-club-football","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"'Another universe': How Indiana football changed Bloomington","description":"The basketball haven has become a legend of the fall, where the reigning national champs take center stage.","published":"2026-11-20T16:31:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50533477/bloomington-indiana-football-town","type":"Story","byline":"Chuck Culpepper","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC standardized NIL, revenue sharing contracts 'unfair' for players, agents say","description":"The SEC's new uniform NIL and revenue sharing agreements are causing an uproar among agents concerned that the contracts are loaded with terms that are unfair.","published":"2026-11-20T01:16:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535591/sec-standardized-nil-contracts-unfair-players-agents-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Waiver approved allowing Army, Navy to play 13th game in 2027","description":"The waiver will allow Army and Navy to play 12 games apiece before the College Football Playoff selections are made and keep their rivalry game.","published":"2026-11-20T14:06:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535192/waiver-approved-army-navy-13th-game-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"James Madison moving to American Conference in 2027","description":"James Madison is leaving the Sun Belt Conference for the American Conference a year earlier than planned, in 2027 rather than 2028.","published":"2026-11-19T21:30:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534149/james-madison-moving-american-conference-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922989/jelani-mcdonald","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelani_McDonald"},"pick":{"pick":40,"round":2,"team":"ARI","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jelani McDonald","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelani_McDonald","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-17T20:11:56Z","intro":"Jelani McDonald is an American college football safety for the Texas Longhorns.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McDonald attended Connally High School in Waco, Texas, where he played both defensive back and quarterback. As a senior, he was the Offensive MVP of District 11-4A Division 2 after rushing 77 times for 852 yards with nine touchdowns, and passing for 707 yards with 13 touchdowns. On defense he had 25 tackles, four sacks and an interception. McDonald was selected to play in the 2023 All-American Bowl. He committed to play college football at the University of Texas at Austin."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Texas in 2023, McDonald played in 12 games and had two tackles. As a sophomore in 2024, he played in 14 games with four starts and recorded 33 tackles and one interception.\nMcDonald became a starting safety his junior year in 2025. In the first four weeks of the 2025 season, McDonald contributed to three turnovers in three consecutive games, logging one fumble recovery for 24 yards against San Jose State, one interception for 16 yards against UTEP, and one interception against Sam Houston. He ended the season with 80 tackles, three interceptions, and one fumble recovery.\nFor the 2026 season, McDonald chose to return for his senior year and continued as the starting safety. In Week 11 against LSU, McDonald recorded three interceptions, becoming the first SEC player to record three interceptions in a single game since 2020. For his performance, McDonald was named Player of the Week by the Associated Press, Chuck Bednarik Award,  Jim Thorpe Award, and Walter Camp Award."}]}}